      "text": "The volume of the cube with edge length six inches is $(6)^3$, while the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is $({12})^3$. The ratio of the two volumes is therefore $\\dfrac{{(6)^3}}{{({12})^3}}$. Replacing $6$ with $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ and $12$ with $2$, we replace them by their common denominator, showing that this ratio is equal to $\\dfrac{{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3}}{{2^3}}$. Simplifying this expression, we have $\\dfrac{{\\dfrac{1}{8}}}{{8}} = \\dfrac{1}{\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 64}}.$ The answer is: 64",
