      "text": "To determine the ratio of the volume of a cube with an edge length of six inches to the volume of a cube with an edge length of one foot, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the volume of the first cube.\n2. Calculate the volume of the second cube.\n3. Find the ratio of the volumes.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the volume of the first cube.**\n\nThe edge length of the first cube is 6 inches. The volume \\( V_1 \\) of a cube is given by the formula:\n\\[ V_1 = \\text{edge length}^3 \\]\nSo, the volume of the first cube is:\n\\[ V_1 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the volume of the second cube.**\n\nThe edge length of the second cube is 1 foot. Since there are 12 inches in a foot, the edge length is 12 inches. The volume \\( V_2 \\) of the second cube is:\n\\[ V_2 = \\text{edge length}^3 \\]\nSo, the volume of the second cube is:\n\\[ V_2 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\n**Step 3: Find the ratio of the volumes.**\n\nThe ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube is:\n\\[ \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{1728} \\]\n\nWe can simplify this fraction by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 1728. The GCD of 216 and 1728 is 216. Therefore, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by 216:\n\\[ \\frac{216}{1728} = \\frac{216 \\div 216}{1728 \\div 216} = \\frac{1}{8} \\]\n\nThus, the ratio of the volume of the cube with an edge length of six inches to the volume of the cube with an edge length of one foot is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}} \\]",
